flstore -- the Software Store
=============================

One window: Explore (home with featured apps, recently updated apps, eight
categories, search, FreeLFS packages), Installed and Updates. It replaces the
Packages app (src/flpackages), which stays only as the provider of
flpkg-seat and is hidden from the menu.

Sources
  Flathub     per user through `flatpak --user` (no root, no polkit): install,
              update, remove, open, "Remove unused runtimes" (also run after
              every removal), update check with `flatpak remote-ls --updates`.
  FreeLFS     the flpkg database. Reads run `flpkg list` and `flpkg search ""`
              as the person; changes go through `flpkg-seat install|remove`.
              Updates are the repo packages flpkg marks "[installed: older]".
              "Check now" also runs `flpkg sync`; if flpkg refuses (it is a
              root command today) the index is simply read again.

The Flathub catalog
  Flathub's appstream collection (11 MB gzip) is downloaded with curl into
  $XDG_CACHE_HOME/flstore/appstream.xml.gz (only when Flathub has something
  newer, at most once a day) and turned into index.tsv (about 0.6 MB, English
  strings only, 3300 apps) and details.bin by `flstore --build-index`, a child
  process that streams the XML (libxml2 reader): 1 second, a few MB of memory.
  The window loads index.tsv; descriptions, screenshot links and licences of
  one app are read from details.bin only when its page opens.
  Icons (64 and 128 px) and screenshots (752 px thumbnails) are downloaded
  one app at a time, only for what is on screen, cached under the same
  directory and decoded to the size they are shown at (at most 10 MB of
  decoded pictures in memory, the screenshot cache is kept under 120 MB).
  Lists are paged (24 cards) and cards outside the window are not drawn, so
  no icon is fetched for them.
  Download and installed sizes come from `flatpak remote-info` when an app
  page opens.

Progress: flatpak's plain output gives "Installing 2/4" steps (a bar that fills
with them, the log under "Show log"); flpkg gives no progress, so that bar
runs as a moving segment. Changes queue; Cancel stops a flatpak change.

Tests
  make check            tests/index.sh: the indexer on a small appstream file
                        (no network, no display).
  tests/store.py        headless flcomp, real Flathub data and pictures,
                        stand-ins for flatpak, flpkg and flpkg-seat: first
                        start, offline, home, category, search, app page with
                        screenshots, install with progress, Installed,
                        Updates, Update all, FreeLFS packages. Screenshots
                        docs/m7/store-*.png. STORE_APPSTREAM=FILE avoids the
                        11 MB download.
Test hooks: FLSTORE_FLPKG, FLSTORE_SEAT, FLSTORE_CONF, FLSTORE_FLATPAK,
FLSTORE_CURL, FLSTORE_SELF, FLSTORE_APPSTREAM_URL, FLSTORE_ICON_URL,
FLSTORE_PAGE=home|cat:N|pkgs|search:TEXT|app:ID|installed|updates. `flstore --updates` opens the Updates tab (flupdate-notify uses it).
FreeLFS package updates come from `flpkg check-updates` (no root needed, it fetches the indexes itself).
